## Installation

Requires Swift 6.1 or later (Xcode 16.3 or later). Supported platforms are iOS 15, macOS 12, tvOS 15 and watchOS 8 or later{% if language.name == 'Swift' %}, plus Linux{% endif %}.

### Xcode

1. In Xcode, select **File > Add Package Dependencies...**
2. Enter `https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName }}` in the search field and select `{{ sdk.gitRepoName }}`.
3. Choose a dependency rule, for example **Up to Next Major Version** from `{{ sdk.version }}`, and click **Add Package**.
4. Add the `{{ spec.info.title | caseUcfirst }}` library to your app target and click **Add Package**.

### Swift Package Manager

Add the package to the dependencies in your `Package.swift`:

```swift
dependencies: [
    .package(url: "https://github.com/{{ sdk.gitUserName }}/{{ sdk.gitRepoName }}", from: "{{ sdk.version }}"),
],
```

Then add the `{{ spec.info.title | caseUcfirst }}` product to your target:

```swift
targets: [
    .target(
        name: "YourAppTarget",
        dependencies: [
            .product(name: "{{ spec.info.title | caseUcfirst }}", package: "{{ sdk.gitRepoName }}"),
        ]
    ),
],
```
